TASK-186.4 runtime harness: the dev toolbar's Web Inspector buttons (Console,
Network, Select Element) on a single tab, in a split (the unfocused pane's
buttons) and in a pane too narrow to dock. Temporary code, never committed to
Detour/. Apply, build, run, revert:

    git apply docs/harness/task186-4-harness.patch && xcodegen generate
    xcodebuild -scheme Detour -configuration Debug build -derivedDataPath .derived
    # $SITE/app.html (console.log, console.warn, fetch('data.json')), api.html,
    # data.json; each page prints innerWidth x innerHeight:
    python3 -m http.server 8864 --bind 127.0.0.1 --directory "$SITE" &
    DETOUR_DATA_DIR=DetourVerify1864 DETOUR_VERIFY_DIR="$OUT" DETOUR_VERIFY_PORT=8864 \
        .derived/Build/Products/Debug/Detour.app/Contents/MacOS/Detour &
    # a watcher captures `screencapture -x -o -l <windowNumber>` for each
    # "SHOOT <name> <windowNumber>" line of $OUT/verify.log; the harness waits
    # for each PNG. Wait for "done" (about 120 s), then kill that pid and the
    # server.
    git apply -R docs/harness/task186-4-harness.patch && xcodegen generate
    rm -r -- ~/Library/Application\ Support/DetourVerify1864

Buttons are pressed with performClick on the group's own buttons, so the
press goes through the window's wiring and the shared WebInspectorToggler;
its onSettled hook logs each decision. After each step the log records
_WKInspector isVisible, where the frontend web view (inspectorWebView) is
(docked in the pane's container, or a window) and the frontend's own
WI.tabBrowser.selectedTabContentView.type.

WebKit stores inspector preferences in the SHARED com.detourbrowser.mac
defaults. Before: only __WebInspectorPageGroupLevel1__.WebKit2InspectorStartsAttached = 1.
The run added ...WebKit2InspectorAttachmentSide (step 8 docks right, then
bottom again); it was deleted afterwards. StartsAttached was unchanged.

Results (2026-10-24, macOS 26.7 25G229, WebKit 21624.5.1.11.3; three runs,
the last one below; every capture read and matching the log; window
1600x900, pane container 1372x900):
- Capabilities 7 (console, network, picker); toolbar stack: copy, separator,
  Console, Network, Select Element.
- 1 Console from closed: show(console); docked bottom in the tab's container
  (inspector 1372x500, page 1372x370 under the 30 pt toolbar), tab "console".
- 2 Console again: close; no frontend web view.
- 3 Network from closed: show(network) after the frontend loaded (~0.1 s
  after the press on a warm process, under 0.4 s cold); tab "network".
- 4 Console while on Network: switchTo(console), tab "console". 4b Network
  while on Console: switchTo(network).
- 5 Network again while on Network: close.
- 5b The user picks Elements inside the inspector (WI.showElementsTab());
  Console then switches (not closes), a second press closes.
- 5c Network then Console in the same turn on a closed inspector: the second
  press retargets the opening one; it opens on "console".
- 8 Docked right through InspectorFrontendHost.requestSetDockSide('right'),
  closed with the button, reopened with Network: docked right again
  (inspector 750x834, page 622x870), i.e. the saved side is kept.
- 6 Picker: on a closed inspector the button turns accent and
  isElementSelectionActive is true while the frontend is connected but in no
  window; pressing again turns it off and WebKit closes the hidden frontend.
  With the inspector open, our button and the inspector's own crosshair are
  both blue. NOT verified: picking an element. Posted NSEvents (app inactive)
  and mouseMoved/mouseDown/mouseUp sent straight to the WKWebView (app active,
  window key) neither highlight nor pick; WebKit's overlay seems to need real
  HID input. A person's click is needed to check that the pick opens Elements
  and the button returns to grey.
- 7 Split (app | api, 672 pt panes, app focused): the api pane's Console
  focused that pane and docked its inspector in the api container (672x500,
  page 672x350, toolbar 672x30); the app pane had no inspector. Network:
  switchTo(network); Network again: close.
- 7d Window narrowed to 1100: api pane 422 pt (< WebKit's 500 pt minimum):
  Console opened the inspector in its own _WKInspectorWindow
  ("Web Inspector — localhost — api.html") on Console; Console again closed it.

